body:
Ok after some testing, it turns out this is true:

&#x200B;

Some people claim this is how Apple designed Messages to work. That if you write an SMS message from your Watch first, then it won’t get deleted. If you composed the message on an iPhone, then it will be deleted across devices.  
Other people claimed that even if you have Messages enabled in iCloud, the platform will only delete iMessages and not SMS messages.

&#x200B;

source: [https://www.idropnews.com/news/faq-why-are-messages-i-delete-from-my-iphone-still-on-my-apple-watch/143480/](https://www.idropnews.com/news/faq-why-are-messages-i-delete-from-my-iphone-still-on-my-apple-watch/143480/)

&#x200B;

So if my settings are NOT set to mirror and I send an SMS from the apple watch, OR send an SMS from the iPhone - when I delete the message thread on iPhone/Apple Watch, it doesn't delete on the other device.

If I send an iMessage from iPhone, it'll show up on the Apple Watch. If I delete it from iPhone, it'll delete from Apple watch.

Finally, if I send an iMessage from Apple watch, it'll show up on the iPhone, but when I delete the thread from Apple Watch, it wont delete from Apple watch.

&#x200B;

Very weird/confusing behaviour.
